[4] (source: chatbot_quick_replies.md)
### Pricing Information

**Sample question:** How much does it cost?

**Response:** The cost for a ninety-minute Premium Jump Pass is twenty-four dollars and ninety cents, while a one hundred and twenty-minute VIP Jump Pass costs twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents. An All Day Pass is priced at thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents. AeroSports grip socks are required, costing three dollars and ninety-nine cents, but they are reusable. Please note that all prices include tax. Go-karting has separate pricing starting at nine dollars and ninety cents. Would you like to proceed with booking?

[5] (source: birthday_parties.md)
## Add-Ons

Birthday party add-ons available at AeroSports Scarborough include large pizzas (cheese, pepperoni, halal pepperoni, vegetarian, or Hawaiian) priced at twenty-five dollars each. Juice boxes are available in packs of ten for thirty dollars, and soft drink cans come in packs of ten for twenty dollars. Physical birthday invitations cost seventy-five cents each. An outside food fee is fifty dollars but is waived for the Ultimate Party. Go kart races can be added for nine dollars and ninety cents per person, already included in the Ultimate Package. A late ordering fee of twenty dollars applies if ordered within twenty-four hours.

[6] (source: jump_prices.md)
## Open Jump Passes

The Premium Jump Pass, suitable for children aged six and older, costs twenty-four dollars and ninety cents for ninety minutes of access to all attractions except Go Karting, Laser Tag, Bazooka Ball, and Mini Golf. For those seeking more time, the VIP Jump Pass offers one hundred twenty minutes at a price of twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents, with the same exclusions.

Children aged two to five can also enjoy these passes. The Premium Jump Pass for this age group is priced at twenty-four dollars and ninety cents for ninety minutes, while the VIP Jump Pass costs twenty-nine dollars and ninety cents for one hundred twenty minutes, both excluding Go Karting, Laser Tag, Bazooka Ball, and Mini Golf.

For those looking for an extended experience, the Ultimate Jump Pass is available to children aged six and older. Priced at forty-nine dollars and ninety cents, it provides one hundred eighty minutes of access to all core attractions. Additionally, jumpers can choose between Go Karting or Mini Golf and Laser Tag or Bazooka Ball.

Children under two years old can enjoy the facilities for free as long as they are accompanied by a paying adult. The duration is the same as that of their accompanying parent's pass.

For unlimited access throughout the day, the All Day Pass is available to all ages at thirty-nine dollars and ninety cents. This pass allows jumpers to enjoy all attractions without time restrictions.

[7] (source: voice_call_scripts.md)
## Go-Karting Overview

We have two go-kart tracks available at AeroSports Scarborough. The main track is suitable for riders who are fifty-four inches or taller and costs nineteen dollars and ninety cents per standalone race, or nine dollars and ninety cents as an add-on if you already possess a jump pass. The mini track accommodates riders who are thirty-six inches or taller, with a standalone cost of nine dollars and ninety cents or four dollars and ninety cents as an add-on. Each race can last up to ten laps. Remember that closed-toed shoes are required for go-karting.


